# RAG1 System Analysis Report

## Executive Summary

**Issue**: When asking "give the vehicle number columns in all tables", the system returns actual vehicle data (rows from tables) instead of returning the column names that represent vehicle numbers across different tables.

**Root Cause**: The schema introspection pattern in [_handle_schema_introspection_query()](file:///Users/algofusion/Documents/dnc_backend_v2/orchestrator/gen_ai/RAG1/sql_generator.py#1233-1406) doesn't match the specific phrasing "vehicle number columns in all tables". The query falls through to the LLM, which misinterprets it as a data query rather than a schema query.

**Impact**: Users cannot discover which columns represent vehicle IDs across different tables, making it harder to understand the data model.

---

## System Architecture Overview

### RAG1 Query Processing Pipeline

```mermaid
graph TD
    A[User Question] --> B{Knowledge Query?}
    B -->|Yes| C[Return Direct Answer]
    B -->|No| D{Schema Introspection?}
    D -->|Yes| E[Generate Schema Query]
    D -->|No| F{Vehicle ID Query?}
    F -->|Yes| G[Use Timeline Template]
    F -->|No| H{Deterministic Pattern?}
    H -->|Yes| I[Use Deterministic Handler]
    H -->|No| J[LLM Generation]
    J --> K[RAG Context Retrieval]
    K --> L[Adaptive Prompt Building]
    L --> M[LLM Inference]
    M --> N[SQL Validation]
    N -->|Valid| O[Execute Query]
    N -->|Invalid| P[Retry with Error Context]
```

### Key Components

1. **[sql_generator.py](file:///Users/algofusion/Documents/dnc_backend_v2/orchestrator/gen_ai/RAG1/sql_generator.py)** (3868 lines)
   - [ProductionSQLGenerator](file:///Users/algofusion/Documents/dnc_backend_v2/orchestrator/gen_ai/RAG1/sql_generator.py#1175-3868): Main orchestrator
   - [AdaptiveLLMGenerator](file:///Users/algofusion/Documents/dnc_backend_v2/orchestrator/gen_ai/RAG1/sql_generator.py#113-1174): LLM-based SQL generation with retry logic
   - Deterministic handlers for common query patterns

2. **[training_data.py](file:///Users/algofusion/Documents/dnc_backend_v2/orchestrator/gen_ai/RAG1/training_data.py)** (12647 lines)
   - `SCHEMA_DESCRIPTIONS`: Complete table and column metadata
   - `DATA_MODEL`: Entity relationships and join rules
   - `TRAINING_QA_PAIRS`: Few-shot examples
   - `SQL_RULES`: Business logic and constraints

3. **[rag_system.py](file:///Users/algofusion/Documents/dnc_backend_v2/orchestrator/gen_ai/RAG1/rag_system.py)**
   - Semantic search using embeddings
   - Context retrieval for LLM prompts

4. **[sql_validator.py](file:///Users/algofusion/Documents/dnc_backend_v2/orchestrator/gen_ai/RAG1/sql_validator.py)**
   - Syntax validation
   - Semantic validation (forbidden joins, column existence)
   - Sanity checks

